"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[62727],{185108:e=>{e.exports="# How to configure historical data backfill\n\nHistorical ingestion runs a Databricks Job that backfills data from **before the `modifiedAfter` cutoff date**. It reads from the same source location as the ongoing autoloader pipeline and writes into the bronze table.\n\n## Prerequisite: modifiedAfter must be set\n\n**Historical ingestion is only meaningful when the datasource has `spec.autoloader.modifiedAfter` configured.**\n\nWhen `modifiedAfter` is set, the ongoing autoloader only picks up files modified on or after that date. Historical ingestion is the complementary job that backfills the data from before that cutoff.\n\nIf `modifiedAfter` is not set, the autoloader already reads all data (current and historical), so a separate backfill job would be redundant. Before enabling historical ingestion, confirm that `spec.autoloader.modifiedAfter` is present in the datasource spec. If it is not set, guide the user to configure `modifiedAfter` first.\n\n## When to suggest it\n\n- User wants to load historical data that predates the `modifiedAfter` cutoff.\n- User asks how to ingest old data or backfill their bronze table, and `modifiedAfter` is already set.\n- User wants to configure the number of parallel shards or concurrency for the backfill.\n\n## Immutability constraint\n\n**`concurrency` and `shardCount` cannot be changed after the datasource is created.** Set these values before the datasource is first published. If they need to change after creation, the datasource must be recreated.\n\n## Enabling historical ingestion\n\nHistorical ingestion is controlled by `spec.autoloader.historicalIngestion`. Set `enabled: true` to start the backfill when the datasource is next applied:\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  autoloader:\n    historicalIngestion:\n      enabled: true\n```\n\n## All configurable fields\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  autoloader:\n    historicalIngestion:\n      enabled: true # Whether to run the historical backfill job\n      concurrency: 1 # Parallel iterations within each shard's job (default: 1, immutable after creation)\n      shardCount: 1 # Number of separate Databricks backfill jobs (default: 1, immutable after creation)\n```\n\n## Choosing concurrency and shardCount\n\n| Scenario                            | Recommendation                                                       |\n| ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Small dataset or testing            | Leave both at defaults (1)                                           |\n| Large dataset, want faster backfill | Increase `shardCount` (e.g. 4–8) to parallelize across multiple jobs |\n| Each shard has many files           | Increase `concurrency` within each shard (e.g. 4)                    |\n| Very large dataset                  | Combine higher `shardCount` and `concurrency`                        |\n\nIncreasing `shardCount` splits the source data across multiple independent jobs. Increasing `concurrency` parallelizes iteration within each job. Both consume more Databricks compute.\n\n## Common configurations\n\n### Enable with defaults (recommended starting point)\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  autoloader:\n    historicalIngestion:\n      enabled: true\n```\n\n### Enable with 4 shards for a large dataset\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  autoloader:\n    historicalIngestion:\n      enabled: true\n      shardCount: 4\n```\n\n### Enable with 4 shards and 2 concurrent iterations per shard\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  autoloader:\n    historicalIngestion:\n      enabled: true\n      shardCount: 4\n      concurrency: 2\n```\n\n### Disable historical ingestion\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  autoloader:\n    historicalIngestion:\n      enabled: false\n```\n\n## Updating via the tool\n\nUse `pageUpdateLakewatchDatasourceSpec` with a partial YAML containing only the `spec.autoloader.historicalIngestion` path. Always summarize the change before calling the tool.\n\nExample to enable with 2 shards:\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  autoloader:\n    historicalIngestion:\n      enabled: true\n      shardCount: 2\n```\n\n## Checking job status\n\nAfter the datasource is applied with historical ingestion enabled, the bronze card shows the per-shard job status (Running, Completed, Error, etc.) with links to the Databricks job. The user can monitor progress there.\n"}}]);
